# Agent shells and the Gradle hooks

Pre-commit runs `./gradlew spotlessCheck`; pre-push runs `./gradlew build`. Agent shells often skip the user's zshrc, so Homebrew OpenJDK is installed but invisible.

## When committing or pushing

1. Pass `required_permissions: ["all"]` on the **first** `git commit` / `git push` that will fire hooks. The sandbox blocks a usable JDK lookup and can force a needless Gradle re-download.
2. If a hook still fails with "Unable to locate a Java Runtime" or a missing
   Java 21 toolchain, export **OpenJDK 21** before retrying — not the
   unversioned `openjdk` formula (that tracks the latest major and may be 26+):

```bash
export JAVA_HOME="/opt/homebrew/opt/openjdk@21"
export PATH="$JAVA_HOME/bin:$PATH"
```

(On Intel Homebrew, use `/usr/local/opt/openjdk@21`.)

   `tools/githooks/with-java.sh` already prefers `@21` and will override a
   pre-set `JAVA_HOME` whose major version is not 21 when `@21` is installed.

3. Do **not** skip hooks (`--no-verify`). Do **not** treat a Gradle distribution fetch (`Downloading https://downloads.gradle.org/...`) as "downloading Java" — the JDK is local; the wrapper is fetching Gradle itself (cached under `~/.gradle/wrapper/dists/` after the first success).
